# Keep the build context minimal. The Dockerfile copies the root manifests by name and the
# whole packages/ folder, and anything that reaches the build stage is in the image's
# history for good: deleting it in a later layer does NOT remove it. A pattern here is
# anchored at the context root unless it starts with **/, which is why every rule below
# does. The first version of this file listed `dist`, `node_modules` and `session.json`
# bare, so they matched only at the root, and the host's build output and node_modules
# under packages/ went into the image (found by the 2026-09-23 audit).
#
# No exceptions, not even for folders that only exist at the root: `**/` also matches at
# the root, and test/dockerignore.test.js fails on any rule that does not start with it.
#
# Every rule in .gitignore above its "Build and tooling" heading has one here too, the
# credentials, everything an archive run writes and the tool's own state files, so a file kept
# out of git by name is kept out of the image the same way; test/dockerignore.test.js checks
# that they agree.
**/.git
**/.claude
**/docs
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.care-album-saver-production
**/care-album-saver-development

# Credentials and personal data.
**/*.har
**/har
**/*.env
**/.env*
**/session.json
**/config.json
**/cookies.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets

# Browser automation state.
**/user-data-dir
**/playwright-state.json
**/storageState.json
**/.playwright

# Photos, and everything an archive run writes beside them.
**/Care*Album*Photos/
**/Brightwheel*Photos/
**/archive
**/downloads
**/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-W[0-9][0-9]
**/archive.json
**/*.xmp
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.png
**/*.gif
**/*.webp
**/*.heic
**/*.heif
**/*.avif
**/*.tif
**/*.tiff
**/*.bmp
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.m4v
**/*.3gp
**/*.webm
**/*.avi
**/*.jpg.json
**/*.jpeg.json
**/*.png.json
**/*.gif.json
**/*.webp.json
**/*.heic.json
**/*.heif.json
**/*.avif.json
**/*.tif.json
**/*.tiff.json
**/*.bmp.json
**/*.mp4.json
**/*.mov.json
**/*.m4v.json
**/*.3gp.json
**/*.webm.json
**/*.avi.json
**/.care-album-saver.lock
**/*.part
**/*_exiftool_tmp
**/*.tmp

# The tool's own state, which lives beside the session in the config folder.
**/photos.json
**/photos.lock
**/photos-handover-*
**/fingerprints.json
**/last-run.json
**/update-check.json
**/daily.log
